  "question": {
    "text": "The spin only magnetic moment of transition metal ion found to be <math>\r <mrow>\r  <mtext>5</mtext><mtext>.92</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>BM</mtext></mrow>\r</math>. The number of unpaired electrons present in the species is:"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Spin only magnetic moment, <math> <mrow> <mtext>μ</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>=</mtext><mtext> </mtext><msqrt> <mrow> <mtext>n(n+2)</mtext></mrow> </msqrt> <mtext> </mtext><mtext>BM</mtext></mrow> </math><br />where <math> <mtext>n</mtext> </math> = no. of unpaired electrons there; <math> <mrow>  <msqrt>   <mrow>    <mtext>n(n</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>+</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>2)</mtext></mrow>  </msqrt>  <mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>=</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>5</mtext><mtext>.92</mtext></mrow></math><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴</mo><mtext>n</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>=</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>5</mtext></mrow> </math>"
  }
